INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES
  ('outdoor-dining-the-benefits-for-your-restaurant', 'The Benefits of Outdoor Dining.', 'If you’re looking for a way to boost your restaurant’s sales during the peak summer months, outdoor dining may be the solution you’ve been searching for. Outdoor dining lets guests feel comfortable and safe while they...', '[{"type":"p","text":"If you’re looking for a way to boost your restaurant’s sales during the peak summer months, outdoor dining may be the solution you’ve been searching for. Outdoor dining lets guests feel comfortable and safe while they enjoy their meal, and it can also help attract new customers who may not have otherwise considered your restaurant."},{"type":"p","text":"In this blog post, we will discuss the benefits of outdoor dining for your restaurant and provide tips on how to create an inviting outdoor space that will encourage guests to stay longer!"},{"type":"p","text":"If you’re not already taking advantage of outdoor dining, now is the time to start! Here are a few benefits of outdoor dining that may convince you:"},{"type":"p","text":"Outdoor dining can help boost your restaurant’s sales during peak summer months."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition to attracting new customers, outdoor dining can also encourage guests to stay longer and spend more money. Guests who are comfortable and enjoying their experience are more likely to order another drink or dessert, or even come back for another meal!"},{"type":"p","text":"Outdoor dining also provides an opportunity for restaurants to stand out from the competition. With so many restaurants vying for attention, anything you can do to make your establishment stand out will give you an edge. An inviting outdoor space is one way to do this, and it’s something that guests will remember long after they’ve left."},{"type":"p","text":"If you’re thinking of adding outdoor dining to your restaurant, there are a few things to keep in mind. First, you’ll need to choose the right location for your outdoor space. It should be close enough to the kitchen so that food can be brought out quickly, but not so close that guests feel like they’re sitting in the way of foot traffic. You’ll also want to make sure there are sufficient dining tables and chairs."},{"type":"p","text":"Once you’ve found the perfect spot for your outdoor dining area, it’s time to start furnishing it! You’ll want to choose furniture that is comfortable and stylish, but also durable enough to withstand the elements. Umbrellas are a must-have for any outdoor dining space, as they provide shade and protection from the sun and rain."},{"type":"p","text":"Creating an inviting outdoor dining space is essential to taking advantage of all the benefits it has to offer. With a little bit of planning and effort, you can transform your restaurant into a summer hot spot! Guests will love being able to enjoy their meal in the fresh air, and you’ll love the boost in sales. Outdoor dining is a win-win for everyone involved!"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_c51532d879874f7baaf40314bad4d1b8~mv2.jpg', 'Restaurant Insights', 'eatOS Staff', '2018-12-20', 'published'),
  ('the-benefits-of-building-an-incredible-team', 'The Benefits of Building an Incredible Team', 'The restaurant industry has an extremely high turnover rate, averaging 75% across the industry according to the Bureau of Labor Statistics. This number is even higher for fast food workers, with a turnover rate closer...', '[{"type":"p","text":"The restaurant industry has an extremely high turnover rate, averaging 75% across the industry according to the Bureau of Labor Statistics. This number is even higher for fast food workers, with a turnover rate closer to 150%."},{"type":"p","text":"So building an efficient, driven, and dedicated staff from the outset leads to better employee retention and saves you the long-term costs of constantly hiring and training new workers."},{"type":"p","text":"One way to build an incredible team is to invest in technology that will help them be more efficient and effective. A point of sale system, for example, can help streamline transactions and reduce errors. It can also provide valuable data that can be used to make informed decisions about staffing levels and menu offerings."},{"type":"p","text":"Building an incredible team is essential to success in the restaurant industry. By investing in technology and making sure your employees have the tools they need to be successful, you can create a foundation for long-term success."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_348f7acd6f984685ac1697599ec1b95d~mv2.jpg', 'Workforce Management', 'eatOS Staff', '2018-12-13', 'published'),
  ('the-future-of-food-cloud-kitchens', 'The Future of Food: Cloud Kitchens', 'With the COVID-19 pandemic causing a surge in quarantines and social distancing across the globe, cloud kitchens have become more popular than ever. But can they really save the restaurant industry?', '[{"type":"p","text":"With the COVID-19 pandemic causing a surge in quarantines and social distancing across the globe, cloud kitchens have become more popular than ever. But can they really save the restaurant industry?"},{"type":"p","text":"Cloud kitchens, also known as ghost kitchens, are commercial kitchens that are used exclusively for the preparation of food for delivery. This means that they don’t have any dine-in or takeout options - you can only order food from them online or through a delivery app."},{"type":"p","text":"While cloud kitchens have been around for a while, the pandemic has caused a boom in their popularity. With more people working from home and avoiding going out to eat, cloud kitchens offer a convenient way to get restaurant-quality food delivered right to your door."},{"type":"p","text":"But can cloud kitchens really save the restaurant industry? It’s hard to say. The pandemic has been devastating for restaurants, with many having to close their doors permanently. And while cloud kitchens may be a godsend for some restaurants, they’re not a perfect solution."},{"type":"p","text":"For one thing, setting up a cloud kitchen can be expensive. Restaurant owners have to pay for commercial kitchen space, as well as the equipment and staff needed to run it. And because they’re delivery-only, they don’t have the same foot traffic as traditional restaurants, which means they may have a hard time generating enough revenue to sustain themselves."},{"type":"p","text":"It’s also worth noting that not all restaurants are suited for the delivery-only model. Fine-dining establishments, for example, wouldn’t do well in a cloud kitchen because their food is meant to be enjoyed in a sit-down setting."},{"type":"p","text":"So, can cloud kitchens save the restaurant industry? Only time will tell. But one thing is for sure: they’re changing the way we think about food delivery."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/86979c_24580a2c4b6a4c6cbbbbf1b7229d8e43~mv2.jpg', 'Kitchen Operations', 'eatOS Staff', '2018-12-06', 'published'),
  ('the-online-fresh-food-revolution', 'The Online Fresh Food Revolution', 'The online fresh food revolution is a direct result of the COVID-19 pandemic. Restaurant kitchens have had to increase their output to meet the demand for takeout and delivery orders, while also accommodating the needs...', '[{"type":"p","text":"The online fresh food revolution is a direct result of the COVID-19 pandemic. Restaurant kitchens have had to increase their output to meet the demand for takeout and delivery orders, while also accommodating the needs of diners who are looking for healthier, fresher options."},{"type":"p","text":"Technology has played a major role in this shift, with apps and online ordering platforms making it easier than ever for customers to get the food they want when they want it. This trend is only likely to continue in the post-pandemic world, as more and more people become accustomed to the convenience of ordering food online."},{"type":"p","text":"While the online fresh food revolution has been driven by the pandemic, it is likely to have a lasting impact on the way we think about food. As we become more aware of the importance of fresh, healthy ingredients, we will be less likely to settle for processed or frozen options. And as we become more accustomed to the convenience of ordering food online, we may never go back to the old way of doing things."},{"type":"p","text":"So what does this mean for the future of food? It means that we are likely to see more restaurants offering delivery and takeout options, as well as more online ordering platforms that make it easy for customers to get the food they want. We are also likely to see a shift towards fresher, healthier ingredients, as people become more aware of the importance of good nutrition. In short, the online fresh food revolution is likely to change the way we think about food forever."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_a8ebe51115a7412b9d2fb734a7017d68~mv2.jpg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2018-11-29', 'published'),
  ('the-tech-solutions-defining-restaurants-future', 'The Tech Solutions Defining Restaurants’ Future', 'Once again, the restaurant industry is changing. The recovery period post-COVID-19 isn’t a linear journey, and so tech solutions are continually coming out to prioritize the new needs of the industry. For example, a...', '[{"type":"p","text":"Once again, the restaurant industry is changing. The recovery period post-COVID-19 isn’t a linear journey, and so tech solutions are continually coming out to prioritize the new needs of the industry. For example, a year ago businesses prioritized social distance and contactless dining. Now they’re relying even more on digitization."},{"type":"p","text":"Customers can get their favorite foods much quicker and more conveniently when they order online. Whether it’s through your website, app or a third party platform, digital solutions provide some safety against the Delta variant and any other curveballs that the pandemic throws next."},{"type":"p","text":"Thanks to the increased reliance on online orders, restaurants can also take a greater interest in their customer data. Smart Point of Sale systems that integrate loyalty programs use customer profiles to track when they come in, what they order and more. Then by analyzing sales data over time, your restaurant will have a better grasp on who your best customers are, how much they spend and when. That informs where your business should place its focus, and which tech solutions to prioritize."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo courtesy of eatOS"},{"type":"h2","text":"The Tech Solutions that Matter Most"},{"type":"p","text":"Moving forward, digitization’s growing role in food service will cause restaurants to consider the long-term costs and benefits. Tech solutions that have good ROI will thrive. Especially because of the labor shortage, automation is more important than ever. Mobile ordering, curbside pickup and ghost kitchens have all risen up to provide good customer solutions."},{"type":"p","text":"Yet just because some face-to-face service is lost, you don’t have to forgo customer satisfaction. Provide order modifications which not only drive profit, but incentivize happy guests to come back. Adaptability is crucial to long-term success, which is why you need access to crucial customer data. Find smart systems that not only track that information, but are as easy to learn and use. Reduce onboarding while improving ordering efficiency, and watch labor costs go down across the board."},{"type":"p","text":"Self-service, though, requires speed and accuracy. Especially with takeout channels, streamlined communication tells customers approximately when their food is ready. Whether they pick it up in-store at their front door, provide the freshest possible meal."},{"type":"h2","text":"Food Service and the Future"},{"type":"p","text":"Technology and digitization will continue playing a large role in food service. As customers get more comfortable with smart tech solutions, POS will keep advancing too. Customers need to know they can rely on your restaurant which is why many smart Point of Sale systems also work in offline mode. When you lose WiFi, your restaurant doesn’t lose connectivity. All of it syncs back safely to the cloud once you’re back online so the flow of operations goes uninterrupted."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS provides a cloud-based system that protects your restaurants and helps it run smoothly. We created an ecosystem of devices that work, because they work together."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant #CloudTechnology"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_b1edda25171045c8956a7923d15b0dff~mv2.jpeg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2018-11-21', 'published'),
  ('why-does-uber-eats-have-a-driver-shortage', 'Why Does Uber Eats Have a Driver Shortage?', 'During the pandemic, restaurants relied on third party apps to deliver their food. Uber Eats is one of the major businesses that restaurants relied on throughout COVID-19.', '[{"type":"p","text":"During the pandemic, restaurants relied on third party apps to deliver their food. Uber Eats is one of the major businesses that restaurants relied on throughout COVID-19."},{"type":"p","text":"Now, however, even the delivery giant has a driver shortage. The reasons for this are multifold. Consider the difficult job of an essential food service worker. They’re busy as the face of both Uber Eats and the restaurant for every customer. When problems occur, they’re the one who get most of the flack."},{"type":"p","text":"Drivers don’t always leave for dire reasons, though. In some cases, they simply found other jobs. Gigs like Uber Eats were necessary during the pandemic, but now that businesses are opening back up, workers can find positions in their preferred fields."},{"type":"h2","text":"Why Restaurants Have Stayed"},{"type":"p","text":"Despite this growing problem, many consumers rely on Uber Eats. Thus restaurants have no choice but to keep using it if they want exposure. Partnering with Uber Eats is marketing in itself. But that’s not enough: Considering the high commissions those apps take, restaurants might not make any money through the app. Yet they hope to convert sales to their direct channels, and it starts with getting noticed there."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo by Charles Deluvio on Unsplash"},{"type":"p","text":"Unfortunately, this presented an issue when the driver shortage began. In late July, many restaurants reported a severe backup of orders, and Uber Eats simply didn’t have the drivers to handle them. Restaurants reported that they got messages about a technical outage, yet the app kept taking orders and not answering repeated phone calls to their help line. Though Uber Eats pays for the orders that fall through the cracks, this is damaging to long-term profits."},{"type":"p","text":"Even worse, their reliance on Uber Eats throughout the pandemic means they don’t have access to a lot of the crucial customer information needed to start their own delivery channels. They don’t get any contact from the customer unless they call asking about their missing food, so it’s harder to track all that data and make informed business decisions."},{"type":"h2","text":"The Uber Eats Driver Shortage Hurts Everyone"},{"type":"p","text":"The company isn’t any happier with the struggle to get couriers, and even customers have felt it. When orders don’t get collected quickly, they go cold or get left at the restaurant completely. If they take too long, people get frustrated and cancel. Some restaurants give out the wasted food to those in need, as food disparity caused by COVID-19 is still very real, but restaurants’ reputations still suffer. Unsatisfied customers won’t come back, and they leave bad reviews which drive away potential new customers. Meanwhile the service workers are getting a lot of the complaints. Considering the labor shortage currently plaguing food service, any additional strain could be disastrous to restaurants."},{"type":"p","text":"If you’re a restaurant looking for an alternative to Uber Eats with all the same great benefits, consider orderOS. We create a delivery app made for you, where you get all the profits and don’t pay any commission. This is extremely helpful for restaurants who want to make a name for themselves and need a hand through the transition."},{"type":"p","text":"#eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #RestaurantBusiness #FoodDelivery #Restaurant #ThirdPartyApps"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_f9e2e33b14c941f3a2b6b9a6fed8ce64~mv2.jpg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2018-11-14', 'published'),
  ('will-a-i-ordering-take-over-food-service', 'Will A.I. Ordering Take Over Food Service?', 'Food service is all about convenience these days. From digital loyalty programs that automatically apply saved points, to online ordering platforms with no-contact delivery, customers value ease of use and fast service....', '[{"type":"p","text":"Food service is all about convenience these days. From digital loyalty programs that automatically apply saved points, to online ordering platforms with no-contact delivery, customers value ease of use and fast service. That’s part of why A.I. technology is gaining popularity across the industry. With smart technology, restaurants are increasing their speed, accuracy and contactless capabilities."},{"type":"p","text":"These machines learn what and why guests order most regularly. Then they make informed, smart, and profitable choices about what to push and upsell. These algorithms show guests what they might like based on past ordering habits, what others enjoy and even the weather."},{"type":"p","text":"Since customers enjoy habit and routine, it reduces some of the burden of choice that comes with having too many options to process. Some worry that the rise in A.I. will limit customers from expanding their palate, but automated suggestions don’t stop them from exploring the full menu if they want to try something new that day. With eatOS Point of Sale, restaurants can also choose menu items to push regardless of customers’ past orders. It’s all designed to improve the dining experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo courtesy of eatOS"},{"type":"h2","text":"Why Customers Love A.I."},{"type":"p","text":"People like having something recommended. Instead of asking their server, now they can get the same experience even when they use self-ordering technology. Smart Point of Sales save customer profiles, so guests can also easily reorder favorite meals or get suggestions based on what they usually like. Combine this data retention with digital rewards programs to accumulate and apply points on any order."},{"type":"p","text":"Sometimes, people walk into a restaurant hungry and with no idea what they’re craving. Advanced A.I. can now make suggestions based on location, popular dishes, the weather, nearby events and what others like. All of this makes a better ordering experience overall. They can also personalize and modify orders to their content with smart self-service devices, so these technologies combine to provide ease-of-use and satisfaction."},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants are benefiting from the push towards digital ordering experiences. Collecting this data lets you better understand customer behavior, analyze long-term trends and get to know guests on a deeper level. This then makes it easier to create marketing initiatives and make business decisions that benefit everyone."},{"type":"p","text":"Photo courtesy of eatOS"},{"type":"h2","text":"The Future of Digital Food Service"},{"type":"p","text":"Predictive ordering isn’t the only part of dining out becoming more influenced by artificial intelligence. For example, Papa John’s made a virtual assistant software named PapaCall, which takes phone orders. A lot of self-service Kiosks now come equipped with voice recognition for in-house ordering without touching the machine at all. Customers just speak and multilingual, touch-free devices let them order, pay and get information just like that."},{"type":"p","text":"As customers get familiar with forward-thinking technology, more restaurants see the benefit of adding smart technology like Kiosks, modern Point of Sales, Kitchen Display Screens and more. That’s why eatOS provides an ecosystem of devices that make restaurant management simple."},{"type":"p","text":"#ArtificialIntelligence #eatOS #PointofSaleforRestaurants #RestaurantBusiness #Restaurant"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/a77ed6_2c3d7b24d79c425f9a84f79a9dbae10b~mv2.jpg', 'Point of Sale', 'eatOS Staff', '2018-11-07', 'published'),
  ('food-business-opportunities-for-sale', 'Food Business Opportunities for Sale', 'The food industry is one of the most popular for businesses. It''s because with or without a pandemic, the food sector is always the number one in-demand business anywhere you go. People eat! a solid reason why it...', '[{"type":"p","text":"The food industry is one of the most popular for businesses. It''s because with or without a pandemic, the food sector is always the number one in-demand business anywhere you go. People eat! a solid reason why it remains visible even in the most challenging times."},{"type":"p","text":"However, opening your restaurant can be difficult. You need to have a proven system to guide your business. That system will make your food business opportunities highly sought after by investors wanting to earn their slice of the high-appraised industry."},{"type":"p","text":"It is not new to everyone that creativity is one factor in starting a business. Anything that you can think of that has to do with food can be a food business opportunity. The multi-billion dollar food industry relates to various establishments that cater to and sell food and beverages. In addition, options in the food business sector include cafes, grocery outlets, delivery services, outdoor and indoor restaurants, catering, and vending machines."},{"type":"p","text":"While the market has become highly competitive, the demand for the food business is so high. Therefore, the most challenging part of the starting process will be planning and designing how your business will stand out from the rest without compromising the options the consumers want."},{"type":"p","text":"It is true that while the popular fast food option may entice a lot of investors, the underrated retail food market is highly profitable too. It includes grocery outlets, convenience stores, food-service contractors, caterers, retail bakeries, beer, liquor, and wine stores. Moreover, the U.S. retail food industry had an estimated $38.96 billion in 2018."},{"type":"p","text":"The fact is, Americans have become more health conscious nowadays. Therefore, investors can expect more healthy options such as light sandwiches and healthy vending. It means you, as the business owner, must include healthy menus. As shown in recent studies, those with healthy dishes on their menu will be able to capitalize on this trend''s success."}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/35ab20_6088139f3e1544439503332187e3afce~mv2.jpg', 'Online Ordering', 'eatOS Staff', '2018-10-31', 'published');
